    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP on this June 4th, our offensive engine is headlined by **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.66) and **Brice Turang** (68.93), both of whom offer the highest efficiency profiles today. **Vinnie Pasquantino** draws a highly favorable matchup against a middling starter, and his platoon-split advantage (+14%) makes him the primary anchor of our lineup. Meanwhile, **Brice Turang** is a priority start despite the catcher's arm; the combination of a weaker opposing pitcher and a clear path to run production from the #3 spot solidifies his value. We are also leaning heavily into the speed element today with **Corbin Carroll** (67.97). Even against a competent lefty, the combination of his #2 spot in the order and a favorable stolen base environment against a slow-delivering pitcher makes him a must-start despite the handedness disadvantage. \n\nThe tightest decision on today's card involved **Travis Bazzana**, who narrowly made the cut with a 45.69 score. While his base projections are solid, the L/L matchup against the starting pitcher creates significant volatility (-9%), leaving him in a precarious position near our roster floor. We are keeping a close watch on **Austin Riley** (42.73) as well; he sits just above the benching threshold, but his score is being suppressed by a tough individual matchup against an elite arm. Should late-breaking news arrive regarding lineup changes or weather, we remain prepared to shift, though for now, we are banking on the projected volume from our core. Note that **Mickey Moniak** and **Giancarlo Stanton** remain sidelined, while **Josh Naylor** and **James Wood** are unavailable due to team off-days, effectively narrowing our depth for today\u2019s slate.",
